## Phase sub-agent

The main session never implements a phase itself. For each phase, from the one Setup step 7 found to the last, it launches one sub-agent with a fresh context, waits for its result, checks it and moves on. Knowledge passes between phases only through the commits, `plan.md` (Progress with SHAs, `## Plan Changes`) and the run report file. A phase whose Automated rows are all checked is skipped; a phase with only Manual rows gets no sub-agent: the main session writes a Skipped entry (`Reason: needs human`) for each of its rows, and they go to the human checklist.

**Launch.** One phase at a time, one sub-agent per phase, through the `Agent` tool (older name `Task`):
- `subagent_type: "general-purpose"`, always named — never `fork`, which inherits the whole conversation instead of a fresh context;
- `model`: the family alias of the session's model, from the exact model ID in the system prompt (`claude-opus-*` → `opus`, `claude-sonnet-*` → `sonnet`, `claude-haiku-*` → `haiku`, `claude-fable-*` → `fable`);
- `run_in_background: false` when the tool has that parameter; when it does not (an interactive session runs sub-agents in the background), wait for the sub-agent's completion notification.

Until the result is in, the main session does nothing else: no edit, no command, no next phase. A prompt in the meantime (e.g. a `/goal` check-in) gets a look at the sub-agent's status and changes nothing. Every state other than a result block takes the "missing or malformed block" path below: no `Agent` or `Task` among your tools, a refused launch, a sub-agent that ended without the block or is stuck. The main session never implements the phase itself and never launches a second sub-agent for it. When TaskUpdate is available, set the phase's task `in_progress` before the launch and `completed` after the checks below pass.

**Prompt.** The sub-agent gets nothing but the prompt, so the prompt carries every path in full (with `${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}` expanded) and every fact from this session:
- this file, `${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}/SKILL.md`, and its `${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}/references/` folder;
- the script `${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}/../10x-impl-review/scripts/validate_change.py`;
- the paths of the plan, `change.md` and the run report file;
- the change-id and the phase number N;
- the bootstrap flag: `yes` when no Progress row before Phase N is checked (the first phase of the change, "Tracking files touched during a phase"), else `no`;
- the paths the main session wrote since the last phase commit, for the touched-file set: the run report file always, `change.md` when Setup changed it, and, for the first phase of this run only, the report file of an interrupted run ("Run report file");
- the `Refs:` line, when the conversation has one ("Tracking issue/task references for commits").

The prompt tells the sub-agent to:
- read fully what "Co czytam" lists for the phase sub-agent, and Setup step 4 and the sections of that `SKILL.md` from "Mismatch taxonomy" to "Manual rows" plus "Progress & state", which are its instructions;
- implement Phase N only: the preflight of its own Automated commands before the first edit (Setup step 4), the mismatch taxonomy with `ADAPT` and `PC<n>` entries, the gate stack, self-fix, the touched-file set (which always holds the plan, the run report file and the paths listed above), the commit ritual, the SHAs in Progress and the phase's Observed entries in the run report file;
- launch no other sub-agent, ask nobody anything, touch no other phase;
- end with the result block below as its only final text.

**Result block**, in this fixed shape:

```
PHASE RESULT — Phase <N>
STATUS: DONE | STOPPED
Model: <exact model ID of the sub-agent>
GATE <name>: PASS|FAIL (...)            (every gate, in order)
COMMIT p<N>: <sha>                       (or "no diff — HEAD <sha>")
ADAPT: ... / PC<n>: ... / DIRTY (not staged): ...   (or "none")
Uncertain: ...                           (for Reported; or "none")
Skipped gates: ...                       (for Skipped; or "none")
Manual rows: <the phase's #### Manual rows verbatim, or "none">
<when STOPPED: the STOP block unchanged and the state of the worktree>
```

**After the result**, the main session:
1. copies the block's `GATE` and `COMMIT` lines (and `ADAPT`, `DIRTY`) into its own response text — the goal evaluator reads only this session's transcript;
2. checks the hard facts in the repo: `git cat-file -e <sha>^{commit}` exits 0, and every Automated row of Phase N in Progress is `- [x]` and ends with ` — <sha>`;
3. writes to the run report file: a Reported entry for each `Uncertain` item and one when `Model` differs from the header's `Model` (the claim names the sub-agent's model); a Skipped entry for each skipped gate and each Manual row (`Reason: needs human`).

A missing or malformed block (including every state listed under "Launch"), or a failed check in item 2, is `STOPPED — GATE FAILURE in Phase <N>` with the evidence (what the block says, what the repo shows): print the STOP block, write item 3 from what the block holds, print the run report and halt. A block with `STATUS: STOPPED` is copied verbatim; then the main session writes item 3, prints the run report and halts. Otherwise it launches the next phase, or goes to "After all phases" after the last one.

The sections from "Mismatch taxonomy" to "Manual rows" below are the phase sub-agent's instructions; their contracts and line shapes do not change. Where they say "your response text", for the sub-agent that is its result block, which the main session copies into the transcript.
